\DOC LOCAL_JMIXADD_TAC

\TYPE {LOCAL_JMIXADD_TAC : int -> tactic}

\SYNOPSIS
Advances an {eventually}-style machine-state goal past a called subroutine,
replacing the state variable by its successor and re-deriving the assumptions
about the new state, including a new correctness assumption about the
subroutine's output buffer.

\DESCRIBE
The single {int} argument is the index N of the state variable: the goal's
current state {sN} is replaced by the next state {s(N+1)} throughout the
conclusion and in the rebuilt assumptions. Exactly one subgoal results. In the
conclusion, only the state term to which the {eventually} predicate is applied
changes; the predicate body is left as is. All assumptions mentioning the old
state are discharged and replaced by corresponding assumptions about the new
state: the program-loaded fact, the register and memory read facts (those
describing the call's argument registers are dropped, and flag facts are
dropped in some cases), and the accumulated {MAYCHANGE} frame, now extended
with further memory components. Two further assumptions give the new
instruction pointer and stack pointer at the return site, and one newly added
universally quantified assumption states the group-law property relating the
subroutine's inputs to the three memory fields it wrote, read in the new state.
Assumptions that do not refer to the state (side conditions, non-overlapping
facts, arithmetic facts, earlier quantified properties) are retained unchanged,
so the newly added quantified property is among the retained assumptions on the
next application.
{
   A, assumptions about sN ?- eventually step (\s. P s) sN
   ========================================================  LOCAL_JMIXADD_TAC N
   A, rebuilt assumptions about s(N+1), (!z1 ... zp. group-law property at s(N+1)) ?- eventually step (\s. P s) s(N+1)
}

\COMMENTS
In all observed traces, only this single kind of transformation occurs, always
on goals of this {eventually}-with-machine-state shape.

\ENDDOC
